{"sequence":11,"at":"2026-09-30T21:14:15.622Z","kind":"dispatch","attemptId":"provider-attempt-6","phase":"initial","transport":"schema-tool","attempt":{"id":"provider-attempt-6","phase":"initial","transport":"schema-tool","status":"pending","startedAt":"2026-09-30T21:14:15.622Z","request":{"messageCount":9,"messageCharacters":35490,"toolNames":["source_list","source_search","source_symbol","source_read","skill_reference_read"],"maxTokens":6000,"executableTools":true,"toolSchemas":[{"type":"object","properties":{"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":[],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":["text"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"startLine":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"endLine":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":["path","startLine","endLine"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"usage":null,"costUsd":null,"transportAttempts":"unknown"}}
{"sequence":12,"at":"2026-09-30T21:14:40.158Z","kind":"response","attemptId":"provider-attempt-6","phase":"initial","transport":"schema-tool","attempt":{"id":"provider-attempt-6","phase":"initial","transport":"schema-tool","status":"response","startedAt":"2026-09-30T21:14:15.622Z","request":{"messageCount":9,"messageCharacters":35490,"toolNames":["source_list","source_search","source_symbol","source_read","skill_reference_read"],"maxTokens":6000,"executableTools":true,"toolSchemas":[{"type":"object","properties":{"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":[],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"text":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":["text"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"startLine":{"type":"integer","minimum":1},"endLine":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"required":["path","startLine","endLine"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"usage":{"input":3994,"output":1191,"cacheRead":16128,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"transportAttempts":"unknown","response":{"text":"## Conformance result: **Conforms**\n\n**No.** An ordinary, non-administrator space member cannot remove a different member. The implementation distinguishes removal of another member from self-removal, consistently with the supplied policy.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n1. `DeleteSpaceMember` requires a current authenticated user, then resolves both:\n   - the caller’s active membership in the named space, and\n   - the target user’s active membership in that same space.  \n   [`server/api/v1/space_service.go:19-27`](ev-fafd545d16e80ba3f154), [`server/api/v1/space_service.go:632-662`](ev-fbee50e39adde963041e)\n\n2. The service compares the target user ID with the current user ID:\n   - **Different member:** it calls `requireSpaceAdministrator(callerMembership)`.\n   - **Self-removal:** it skips that administrator check.  \n   [`server/api/v1/space_service.go:740-760`](ev-f8bff7bba8aba4838cb4)\n\n3. `requireSpaceAdministrator` accepts only a membership whose role is exactly `SpaceMemberRoleAdmin`; an ordinary member receives `PermissionDenied`.  \n   [`server/api/v1/space_service.go:54-58`](ev-fafd545d16e80ba3f154)\n\n4. The datastore independently repeats the distinction:\n   - when `actorUserID != delete.UserID`, the actor must have an active administrator membership;\n   - when the IDs are equal, this administrator requirement is not applied.  \n   This is present in all three visible database implementations:\n   - PostgreSQL: [`store/db/postgres/space.go:437-466`](ev-a4a9b3ec660e85b8b8ea)\n   - MySQL: [`store/db/mysql/space.go:399-428`](ev-c8e210c550cddb59c043)\n   - SQLite: [`store/db/sqlite/space.go:411-433`](ev-5a78461a01f2daec62fb)\n\nThus, an ordinary member trying to remove another member is denied at both the API service layer and the database layer.\n\n### Admin versus self-removal paths\n\nThe paths visibly differ:\n\n| Operation | Required authority |\n|---|---|\n| Remove another member | Active space administrator |\n| Remove oneself | Active membership; administrator role not required |\n\nBoth paths nevertheless share a separate invariant: deletion is rejected if it would remove the last active administrator. For example, PostgreSQL counts active normal-user administrators and returns `ErrLastSpaceAdmin` when only one remains. [`store/db/postgres/space.go:467-486`](ev-a7f97cc0372b21deca98) Equivalent checks appear in MySQL and SQLite. [`store/db/mysql/space.go:429-448`](ev-c8e210c550cddb59c043), [`store/db/sqlite/space.go:434-454`](ev-5a78461a01f2daec62fb)\n\nConsequently, the policy permits self-removal, but the implementation may prevent a self-removing administrator from leaving when doing so would leave the space without an active administrator. That is an additional integrity restriction, not permission for ordinary members to remove others.\n\nThe API contract also explicitly documents self-removal: “A member may delete their own membership to leave the space.” [`proto/api/v1/space_service.proto:126-130`](ev-569b31010d753cffda2f)\n\n### Policy comparison\n\nSupplied policy:\n\n> Only a space administrator may remove another member from that space. This policy does not prohibit a member leaving the space themselves.\n\nThe source enforces both elements:\n\n- non-self deletion requires the caller’s exact space role to be administrator;\n- self-deletion bypasses that administrator requirement.\n\n**Conclusion:** source-visible behavior conforms to the independently supplied policy.\n\n### Decisive limits\n\nThis was a bounded source-only review. The inspected code establishes authorization after `fetchCurrentUser(ctx)` supplies the current user. The source evidence reviewed here does not establish how deployment middleware authenticates the request or binds request credentials to that context identity, so no claim is made about identity spoofing resistance or undocumented role grants. No such middleware or grants were assumed. The Connect handler itself merely delegates to this service and adds no alternate visible authorization path. [`server/api/v1/connect_services.go:650-655`](ev-2218ecb61f39c5805d25)","toolCalls":[],"tokens":{"input":3994,"output":1191,"cacheRead":16128,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"durationMs":24536.237,"stopReason":"end_turn"},"endedAt":"2026-09-30T21:14:40.158Z"}}
